2026‑3388) |\n| **4. Claims‑bordereau summary – Pearson Hardman Underwriting (June 2026)** | Part of a broader underwriting summary; it notes that three claims in the month exceeded the £25 k settlement authority and were referred for liability assessment. No indication that TM‑2026‑0031 was among those three, but the board’s reference to “claims above the reference threshold” suggests the insurer is monitoring similar thresholds. | *Claims bordereau summary, Pearson Hardman Underwriting, June 2026* (generic, not specific to TM‑2026‑0031) |\n\n### What needs a reply?\n\n1. **Marbury Wills LLP’s disclosure request** – The claim is *still open* (status = open) and the solicitors have explicitly requested the full claim file within **seven days**. No acknowledgement or response has been recorded in the claim system, so a reply is required (or at least a note confirming receipt and a timeline for delivery).\n\n2. **Ashgrove Adjusting’s investigation** – While the loss‑adjuster report is already part of the claim record, the solicitor correspondence does not indicate any follow‑up questions. If the insurer wishes to discuss any aspects of the report (e.g., contractor’s actions, timeline of repairs), a brief reply would be prudent, but nothing urgent is flagged at this stage.\n\n3. **Redwell Restoration invoice** – The invoice has been attached to the claim; payment has been made, so no further action is required from the claims handler.\n\n### Action recommendation\n\n- **Reply immediately** to Marbury Wills LLP confirming receipt of their disclosure request and outlining the date by which the full claim file (including all handling notes) will be supplied, preferably within the next seven days.\n\n- Review whether any additional information is needed from Ashgrove Adjusting (e.g., a brief clarification on the contractor’s role) – this can be done once the solicitor correspondence is acknowledged, but it is not currently flagged as urgent.\n\nAll other documents (invoice, bordereau summary) are already part of the claim record and do not require further response at this time.", "response_hash": "sha256:29c7bde5ea5a23cf0acdba86b7a0087096c4810eaf08bfe46023643789640c5d", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
